  "entry": "code/web/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Find moving asteroids in a set of same-field telescope FITS frames, either with an automated align-detect-track pipeline or by ear with a sonified shift-and-stack hunt. It also ranks tonight's near-Earth asteroid targets, shows their 3D orbits and hazard figures, and pools RA/Dec observations from several observers into a Gauss-method orbit fit. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
